'''CyberFace''' (メタルカオル君 ''Metaru Kaoru-kun'') is a [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] variant of [[The Face]] that appears in [[Legend Stages]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = CyberFace
|image = E 058.png
|first appearance = [[Steel Visage (Deadly)|Facing Danger]]<br>
'''SoL''': [[Knights of the Round|Sub-chapter 28 - Knights of the Round]]
|latest appearance = '''ZL''': [[Uneducated Sophist|Sub-chapter 9 - Uneducated Sophist]]
|money drop = 550¢ - 2,172¢
}}

==Enemy==
CyberFace has insane attack power, very low health, high speed, a 90% chance to create a Lv.8 [[Wave Attack]] reaching to a range of 2,135, a 30% chance to [[Knockback|knockback]] cats, and the [[Base Destroyer]] ability. Its only weaknesses are [[Critical Hit]]s and its slow attack rate, meaning most [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critical Hitters]] will easily one-shot CyberFace if given the opportunity.

It is often used similarly to [[Assassin Bear]] as a makeshift time limit or failure condition, typically being spammed after a certain amount of time has passed, or when the enemy limit is not kept filled. For that purpose, it also has the added property of not being vulnerable to the [[Cat Cannon]] or most lucky/lingering attacks.

While it may look like a [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemy, it's actually walking - according to its description, its dozen plasma legs are invisible to the player.

==Strategy==
Using [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shields]] like [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] will allow your Critical Hitters to have a chance of hitting CyberFace without getting decimated by its wave. [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Hurricat]] completely obliterates CyberFace due to his insanely high probability of [[Critical Hit]]s. Just remember not to completely rely on him, as he will perish instantly if he doesn't crit.

[[Rei Uzumasa & Cat (Special Cat)|Rei Uzumasa & Cat]], [[Sunny Neneko (Super Rare Cat)|Sunny Neneko]], or [[Cheerleader Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cheerleader Cat]] can annihilate CyberFace 100% of the time, but be sure to keep them from wasting their attacks on anything else. [[Crazed Moneko (Special Cat)|Crazed Moneko]] can also work, but due to her long foreswing and low range, she won't be as effective as the others. [[Million-Dollar Cat (Special Cat)|Million-Dollar Cat]] can take out a 100% CyberFace in two attacks with its guaranteed Crits, or one if above level 46.

[[Li'l Cow Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Lion Cat]] can keep this enemy far enough away from the [[Cat Base]] to prevent a game over if timed well, plus his rapid attacks can deal some good damage. Be wary though, for a poorly timed Li'l Lion can cause a massive gap in the line of defense. [[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Cat]] is very effective against CyberFace, as he requires a set amount of hits to be killed. This allows you to get another cat behind Metal Cat that can deal enough damage to kill the CyberFace, but be wary, as CyberFace's knockback ability can push Metal Cat back.

